{"author":{"id":"7c4447400584c47aa149f6e8214e560c5ba23d94ed2431d1d20a80821b0e2113"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792333968,"nonce":"iDtzSea+N80d5hR1Darv2qXofxc=","title":"A page can play audio: a browser MediaPlayer for xavi and hlavi","message":"**Why**\nashui's media package (Audio, Video, Player) drives hlavi's MediaPlayer. hlavi does not build for wasm (src/lib.rs stops with a compile_error), so a program in a page has no media at all. ashui's landing-page demo needs real music in a browser.\n\n**What**\nA browser backend for xavi's MediaPlayer, built as xwindow and xgpu are: the program's side module (xavi.wasm, from hlavi) sends commands through a mailbox to a page agent (xavi.mjs) that the host starts with ash_host_agent, and the agent runs them on an HTMLMediaElement. The state a program reads (state, position, duration, volume) is kept by the agent in shared memory, so reading it is not a call.\nAutoplay: a browser lets play() through only after the user has interacted; the agent holds a play request until the next input, as xwindow's agent does for fullscreen and the clipboard.\nEverything else in the xavi surface (codecs, muxers, queues, AudioData) is not available in a page for now and raises that, as xwindow's unimplemented calls do. The CPU operations could be built for wasm later; the codecs could use WebCodecs.\n\n**Scope of the first step**\nAudio files by URL, relative to the page: open, state, position, duration, volume, play, pause, seek, set volume, close. No equalizer, no video frames yet (pollFrame is false).\n\n**Checks**\nA program in headless Chrome opens a file, plays it and sees the position advance, pauses, seeks, ends; ashui's Player and the dashboard demo use it.","files":null}]}